# Fast Decisions, Costly Forgetting

Begin with the central distinction: [complexity theory](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computational_complexity_theory) classifies how resources grow, while [Landauer’s principle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landauer%27s_principle) prices information that is discarded.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

The first widget turns $W_{\min}=NkT\ln2$ into a tangible scale. Explore temperature and memory size before opening the derivation.

<details><summary>Reveal the one-bit mean-work argument</summary>
For a finite probability distribution $p_i$, Jensen’s inequality and the Jarzynski equality give
$$e^{- eta\sum_i p_iW_i}\leq\sum_i p_i e^{- eta W_i}=e^{- eta\Delta F}.$$
Since $ eta>0$, this implies $\sum_i p_iW_i\geq\Delta F=kT\ln2>0$.
</details>

