<details><summary>Reveal why the second work value is forced</summary>
With equal probabilities, $kT=1$, and $\Delta F=\ln2$, the equality is $(e^{-W_1}+e^{-W_2})/2=1/2$. Hence $W_2=-\ln(1-e^{-W_1})$.
</details>

## The complexity bridge

A problem is hard for a class when every member reduces to it. Under the [extended Church–Turing thesis](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church%E2%80%93Turing_thesis), a physically polynomial hard target is machine-polynomial; closure under reductions then propagates that status throughout the class.

