<details><summary>Reveal the collapse proof</summary>
Let $D$ be hard for $\mathcal N$ and physically polynomial. The simulation inclusion gives $D\in\mathcal P$. For each $A\in\mathcal N$, hardness gives $A\leq_m D$, and reduction closure gives $A\in\mathcal P$. Thus $\mathcal N\subseteq\mathcal P$; with $\mathcal P\subseteq\mathcal N$, the classes are equal.
</details>

