A collapse can make the decision efficient. It does not turn the reset map $0\mapsto0$, $1\mapsto0$ into an injective map. Under the stated finite positive-temperature dynamics, it also cannot make mean erasure work vanish. For more background, see the [Jarzynski equality](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jarzynski_equality) and [reversible computing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reversible_computing).
